    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the number of odd numbers with distinct digits between 100 and 999, we must choose four distinct digits out of the ten available and arrange them in ascending order to ensure all digits are used.\nThere are ${10 \\choose 4} = \\frac{10!}{4!6!} = 210$ possible combinations of four distinct digits.\nFor each combination, we need to choose which digit will be the leading digit (e.g. 7341 will have 7 as the leading digit)\nThere are 5 choices for the leading digit (1-6), and for each choice of leading digit, the third digit can be any of the remaining 9 digits.\nTherefore, the total number of odd numbers with distinct digits is 210 x 5 x 9 = \\boxed{8100}.The answer is: 8100",
